# rule.always.defer-fulcrums-to-last

a design fulcrum surfaces mid-drive: best-guess it, flag it, drive on. fulcrum review is one council at the end.

| the fulcrum is | you |
|---|---|
| impliedly answered by the wish or a reviewer | take that answer |
| open, rework **clean** | best-guess, note why, flag for the end |
| open, rework **dirty** | `--as blocked`, last and named |

clean = rename, swapped default, re-scoped boundary, no ripple. dirty = callers hardened against it or later work built on it (reversal is a teardown).

unsure → treat as clean and flag. a block needs all three: no defensible guess · dirty rework · every other question addressed.

record: `rule.always.itemize-the-fulcrums-you-best-guess`.
